# Pinned upstream Proton Mail Bridge release.
#
# Update with: scripts/update-bridge.sh [VERSION]
# The script downloads the .deb from proton.me, verifies Proton's embedded
# package signature with the committed key in keys/, resolves the release's
# source and Go version, and rewrites this file. Commit the result.
#
# BRIDGE_VERSION        upstream version, without the "-1" Debian revision
# BRIDGE_DEB_SHA256     sha256 of protonmail-bridge_${BRIDGE_VERSION}-1_amd64.deb
# BRIDGE_SIGNING_KEY    full 40-digit fingerprint of Proton's Bridge signing key.
#                       The image build refuses a package not signed by this key.
# BRIDGE_SOURCE_H1      Go checksum-database hash of the release's source
#                       (github.com/ProtonMail/proton-bridge/v3@vVERSION). The
#                       source build refuses anything else.
# BRIDGE_SOURCE_COMMIT  the commit the release tag points at (recorded in the
#                       binary as its revision; cross-checked with GitHub)
# GO_TOOLCHAIN          the exact Go release the source build uses
#
BRIDGE_VERSION=3.27.2
BRIDGE_DEB_SHA256=cf08332dcc4a332c3592476855e2007e6daadbcdac11fab6af83470a3255a8dc
BRIDGE_SIGNING_KEY=D51E64D3E63EDC3EEF7864CEE2C75D68E6234B07
BRIDGE_SOURCE_H1=h1:luK0q/iRiKFWwUa467+4fLW8Sf2B77sHnp5Gp75+RFM=
BRIDGE_SOURCE_COMMIT=3e9f85aa3c676a573b64b1d90829970ded26dbfa
GO_TOOLCHAIN=go1.26.11
